(Section 2\(d\). Definition of Consideration) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 610.8899999999999864 Td
(When, at the desire of the promisor, the promisee or any other person has done or abstained from doing, or does or abstains from) Tj
T* (doing, or promises to do or to abstain from doing, something, such act or abstinence or promise is called a consideration for the) Tj
T* (promise.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 551.8899999999999864 Td
(CHAPTER II - OF CONTRACTS, VOIDABLE CONTRACTS AND VOID AGREEMENTS) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0 g
40. 533.8899999999999864 Td
(Section 10. What Agreements Are Contracts) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 517.8899999999999864 Td
(All agreements are contracts if they are made by the free consent of parties competent to contract, for a lawful consideration and) Tj
T* (with a lawful object, and are not hereby expressly declared to be void.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 471.8899999999999864 Td
(CHAPTER II - VOID AGREEMENTS) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0 g
40. 453.8899999999999864 Td
(Section 27. Agreement in Restraint of Trade Void) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 437.8899999999999864 Td
(Every agreement by which any one is restrained from exercising a lawful profession, trade or business of any kind, is to that) Tj
T* (extent void. Exception 1: One who sells the goodwill of a business may agree with the buyer to refrain from carrying on a) Tj
T* (similar business.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 378.8899999999999864 Td
(CHAPTER VI - OF THE CONSEQUENCES OF BREACH OF CONTRACT) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0 g
40. 360.8899999999999864 Td
(Section 73. Compensation for Loss or Damage Caused by Breach of Contract) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
40. 344.8899999999999864 Td
(When a contract has been broken, the party who suffers by such breach is entitled to receive, from the party who has broken the) Tj
T* (contract, compensation for any loss or damage caused to him thereby, which naturally arose in the usual course of things from) Tj
T* (such breach, or which the parties knew, when they made the contract, to be likely to result from the breach of it.) Tj
